\ dd.frac -- two-component rational expansions (hi lo), not IEEE double-double.
\ A value is represented as the *unevaluated exact sum* hi + lo. Each component
\ must itself be representable as a bounded Rat. This extends representable
\ sums without widening the core, but is NOT a general 30-digit float, and
\ operations can still yield bottom when individual components overflow.
\ The component pair remains on the stack. Requires no new C primitives.
def dd+ :dd-blo :dd-bhi :dd-alo :dd-ahi dd-ahi dd-bhi + dd-alo dd-blo + ;
def dd- :dd-blo :dd-bhi :dd-alo :dd-ahi dd-ahi dd-bhi - dd-alo dd-blo - ;
def dd-neg :dd-lo :dd-hi dd-hi neg dd-lo neg ;
def dd* :dd-blo :dd-bhi :dd-alo :dd-ahi dd-ahi dd-bhi * dd-ahi dd-blo * dd-alo dd-bhi * + dd-alo dd-blo * + ;
def dd-int* :dd-scale :dd-lo :dd-hi dd-hi dd-scale * dd-lo dd-scale * ;
\ Print each exact component separately, rather than overflowing by folding.
def dd. :dd-lo :dd-hi dd-hi . dd-lo . ;
\ dd-collapse works only when hi+lo fits a single core Rat.
def dd-collapse + ;
